{"id": "EUVD-2026-103545", "enisaUuid": "2120deaf-d86a-3c00-91ba-4e3a61c0029e", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nxsk: Use a 32-bit compare in xsk_map_gen_lookup\n\nxsk_map_gen_lookup() loads a u32 key and compares it with max_entries\nusing BPF_JMP_IMM. BPF immediates are sign-extended to 64 bits, so a\nmax_entries value of 0x80000000 or higher becomes a threshold larger\nthan every zero-extended 32-bit key. An out-of-range index then skips\nthe bounds check and the generated lookup reads past xsk_map[].\n\nCompare with BPF_JMP32_IMM so the check stays in 32-bit unsigned range.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:19:53", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:22:59", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c6d5c582d55a8f229d75e98d62eaa065b0deb18d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/227ec890559e922e235eb543646e3bf0bd8269b0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/11d9be35c1f4233798e99be98bc474f83a254c6c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/123f90f394ca404ab8796a7c8072ff7fa5b65a9c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/36461e58f88a1b723f86693f437ac12e60ff4363", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b5c0cff0c5331582ab01c4c423731453a8381acc", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3c1e0a4bc156b8d5c5772dbc76b9ea74dce5ca24", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/70504de0bb627848667207bec7ccfd647deb8814"], "aliases": ["GHSA-r8m8-f9qq-5h53", "CVE-2026-98631"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1183102a-28d0-3b55-925b-03187b28c9b9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e65650f291ee72fc578d6346080fc4699204ef2c <c6d5c582d55a8f229d75e98d62eaa065b0deb18d"}, {"id": "2cfc9aa2-3e9b-3516-a6ec-a7ffeb41dfb3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.10.271"}, {"id": "3f23f8d6-3e70-3f88-831f-430b4459189a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.55"}, {"id": "523da3ef-5db3-39b8-9cd